{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1 — proven root cause)\n\n**Confirmed mechanism.** `src/rebar/config.py::reconciler_repo_root()` resolves the reconciler's default repo root (when `REBAR_ROOT` is unset) as `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]` — the *package location*. This yields the checkout **only** under an editable install, where the package physically lives inside the checkout. Under a non-editable / wheel install the package lives in `site-packages`, so `parents[2]` is a venv path (`<venv>/lib/pythonX`) that is **not a checkout** — returned silently as the repo root.\n\n**Discriminating proof (runtime, `REBAR_ROOT` unset).**\n- Editable/source `config.__file__ = .../fix-c0b9-repo-root/src/rebar/config.py` → `parents[2] = .../fix-c0b9-repo-root` → `.git` present ✔, `src/rebar` present ✔ (a real checkout).\n- Non-editable `config.__file__ = <venv>/lib/python3.13/site-packages/rebar/config.py` → `parents[2] = <venv>/lib/python3.13` → `.git` absent �’, `src/rebar` absent ✗ (NOT a checkout).\n\nThis is the exact CI failure: `Resolved repo_root PosixPath('/Users/runner/work/rebar/rebar/.venv/lib/python3.13') does not contain src/rebar/...`. Production is unaffected only because it always sets `REBAR_ROOT`; the mirror sweep's non-editable + floor legs (which unset it) expose the defect. `invariants._default_repo_root()` just delegates to this resolver, and all 13 reconciler sites reach it, so the wrong value would silently point the whole pass at a non-existent tree.\n\n**Legitimacy = `defect`** (cited authoritative sources):\n1. The function's own docstring **design invariant** — a CWD-independent root for the daemon — is not met: a venv path is not a usable checkout root.\n2. Existing test contract `test_reconcile_main.py::_assert_resolved_repo_root` asserts the resolved root contains `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`; it cannot hold once installed non-editably.\n3. Prior closed bug `e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a` documents this as a **production** behavior defect (distinct from the test-side packaging fixes it split off).\n\n**Defect origin / attribution.** The package-location-as-default was *born* in bootstrap commit `b534f47a` (\"Extract DSO ticket system + Jira reconciler into standalone rebar\", 2026-06-08, the repo's 3rd commit) as `__main__.py`'s `REBAR_ROOT or PROJECT_ROOT or Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]` — **no `rebar-ticket:` trailer** (pre-convention bootstrap; unattributable to a ticket). It was then **deliberately re-established** as the owned, documented `reconciler_repo_root()` default by **C3a-CORE `d361eb28`** (`rebar-ticket: ba8b-c728-8c62-48e9`, \"RP-04 C3a-CORE: cut reconciler core config reads\", 2026-08-19), which authored the current defective line (`parents[2]`), articulated the CWD-independence design in the docstring, and could plausibly have caught the non-editable case in review. Per the carrier rule (C3a-CORE moved `parents[4]`→`parents[2]` preserving package-location semantics) the mechanical bootstrap origin is a carrier; I attribute to the **deliberate owned-default design `ba8b`** as `plan_defect` — the most recent, ticketed, reviewer-vettable decision that owns the line — and record the bootstrap origin here so the full chain survives. `caused_by` link recorded; `--caused-by=ba8b-c728-8c62-48e9` will be passed on close.\n\n**Caller-dependency sweep.** All callers (`invariants._default_repo_root` → 13 reconciler sites) *expect a real checkout*; none relies on the wrong venv path (it would fail downstream anyway). The approved fix only ever returns a validated checkout or raises — strictly safer. Only-incidental usage → proceeds to Phase 2.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788131153781979532,"uuid":"b0bd039b-80ec-4ae8-b4c9-aa1cd7f83b73"}